## 3. Surviving Question and Claim Ceiling

**Reframed Gate 1 question (one sentence):**

On instances from an existing or minimally extended DEL-based epistemic-game family with an independently audited formal verifier and confirmed text-to-model faithfulness, does a trigger-matched strategy card improve verified answer accuracy on valid-applicability (S1) instances relative to a content-length-matched prose control, and — separately, as a secondary registered contrast — does including obligation text reduce error rates on invalid-applicability (S2) instances relative to an otherwise-identical card without obligations?

**Claim ceiling:** A positive result would show that *this specific prompt package* adds value on *this specific family* over a matched control. It would not establish a general retrieval mechanism, recursive reasoning, theory of mind, or generalization to other task families. The obligation sub-claim is a *separate* finding requiring its own comparison; it cannot be inferred from the S1 result.

