If both arrive and the question is simultaneously narrowed to the single-sentence reframe above (separating the primary P−L contrast from the secondary obligation contrast, reclassifying H4/H5, and adding the missing prior-work entry), I would revise to PASS.

### Strongest argument for ABORT/CLOSE

One could argue that MindGames + Hi-ToM + "Beyond Memorization" collectively cover the Q-A space so thoroughly that there is no room for a novel family. I do not find this persuasive because none of these papers study a *strategy-card intervention* with *obligation text* on *validity-stratified instances*. The Q-B intervention is structurally distinct from what any identified prior work evaluates. The question is wounded on Q-A but alive on Q-B.

